, goal_line, prevent; = base; - cover2; -- man.\n- pass_medium: intermediate throw, 10-18 yards. vs defenses: ++ cover2, goal_line; + base, cover3; = man; - prevent; -- blitz.\n- pass_deep: deep shot, 20+ yards (interceptions when it loses). vs defenses: ++ man, goal_line; + blitz; = base; - cover3; -- cover2, prevent.\n- screen: screen to the RB behind the rush. vs defenses: ++ blitz; + cover3, goal_line, prevent; = cover2; - base; -- man.\n- play_action: fake run, then a medium throw (better once 40%+ of your plays have been runs, worse if you never run). vs defenses: ++ base, goal_line; = cover2, cover3, man; - prevent; -- blitz.\n- punt / field_goal: kick (choose them yourself on 4th down; a field goal beyond your kicker's range usually misses). Without a valid answer on 4th down you kick.\n- kneel: run out the clock (when ahead late). spike: stop the clock (costs a down).\n- target: preferred receiver for passes (wr1 is the best receiver; \"\" lets the QB choose).\n- tempo: hurry = no huddle, ~12 s between plays (when behind late); milk = use the whole play clock (when ahead late); normal otherwise."},{"n":64,"side":0,"situation":"You are the OFFENSE of Challenger. Q2 6:09 left in the quarter. Score: Challenger 7 - Bot Rookie 20.\nDown: 1 & 10 at the offense's own 28. Timeouts: you 3, them 3.\nA field goal from here would be 89 yards (your kicker's range is ~53).\nTheir DEFENSE so far: overall: base 13%, cover2 22%, cover3 18%, man 40%, goal_line 4% (22 plays); on 1st down: base 20%, cover2 40%, cover3 20%, man 20% (10 plays); on 3rd & 5+: man 100% (1 plays); last plays: 2&5 cover2 | 1&10 man | 2&8 cover3 | 3&2 goal_line | 4&2 man | 1&10 base.\nYour offense so far: overall: run_inside 18%, run_outside 13%, pass_short 18%, pass_medium 13%, pass_deep 27%, play_action 9% (22 plays); on 1st down: run_inside 40%, run_outside 10%, pass_short 20%, pass_deep 20%, play_action 10% (10 plays); on 3rd & 5+: pass_deep 100% (1 plays); last plays: 2&5 pass_deep | 1&10 run_ins